paths: file:v3/src/Loader.scala file:v3/src/Parser.scala file:v3/src/Source.scala mod:v3/tests/front file:BUGS.md file:v3/SPRINT.md
scope: |
  `import a.b.C` maps onto the markdown-link module mechanism instead of being refused.
  MEASURED FIRST: of 10 lines in corpus+std that begin with `import`, 7 are a bare dotted path
  and only 3 of those are CODE — the other 4 are inside ```text doc fences, so the rule must be
  fence-aware or it imports a documentation example. The two real ones are
  tests/conformance/actors-{bounded-mailbox,process-info}.ssc; the third is `import std.geo.*`
  in std/geo.ssc, a SELF-import (harmless: Loader.visit marks `seen` before recursing).
  Also found: uniml ACCEPTS both files (rc=0) while v3 REFUSES them — a front capability
  divergence that front-capability-gate.sh cannot see, because it reads bench/corpus and these
  two live in tests/conformance.
next: Loader derives the target, Source blanks the line, Parser refuses only unsupported forms
